 "text": "Hi, how you doing right now? Starting with a light layer gives the best result. A tinted moisturiser is good place to start, or a matte foundation that's very neutral. Yes, in your normal direction. Mixing it in a bowl makes it easier to control. Use shades that are a bit cooler, so if you're orangey, go for something slightly cooler and less olive. For a single shade, yes. For mixing different shades, dabs them on with small brush and blend gently. Blending is the key. Use a soft brush with a little shadow shadow and blend from the sides in a circular motion.",
